<!--Post: 1871--><!--Time: 1103063656-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1871"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksugirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksugirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 2:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I posted the following on Kansas.com.  Tom, have you heard this before?  Anyone else?  Thanks.  <BR> <BR>I apologize in advance if this topic has been addressed before on this board. I just finished reading a book entitled LITTLE GIRL FLY AWAY, by Gene Stone, about Ruth Finley, a Wichita resident who gained notoriety as &#34;The Poet&#34; in the late 70&#39;s and early 80&#39;s. BTK is covered somewhat in the book, as Mrs. Finley resided near some of the murder locations and her psychiatrist believes that anxiety relating to BTK may have been partially responsible for Mrs. Finley&#39;s dissociations into &#34;The Poet.&#34; In the book, Mr. Stone states that LaMunyon had a pretty good idea of who BTK was in the mid 80&#39;s, but was never able to arrest him. I am wondering if anyone else on this board has heard this information before, and knows of any further details. Thanks so much. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1871-->
<!--Post: 1873--><!--Time: 1103064916-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1873"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 2:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s news to me, although I know quite a few of the original suspects have since been eliminated via DNA.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1873-->
<!--Post: 1922--><!--Time: 1103127089-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1922"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksugirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksugirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 8:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The book was published in 1994.  At that time, the general opinion was, of course, that BTK was dead, in prison, etc., never to be heard from again, so LaMunyon probably felt free to voice his theory.  I doubt he would be so forthcoming now.  Would be interesting to know if this person has been swabbed.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1922-->
<!--Post: 1939--><!--Time: 1103152053-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1939"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pilot<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pilot<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 3:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just a funny side to this:  A co-worker thinks BTK is either Retired Police Chief Richard LaMunyon or Retired Sheriff Johnny Darr. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1939-->
<!--Post: 2142--><!--Time: 1103338447-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2142"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oliver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oliver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 6:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My father was an executive at Beach AirCraft. Retired now. But, he said he worked with a lady that had worked with the Sheriff&#39;s dept. and she told him that they &#40;the authorities&#41; knew who it was but that his mother had given him an alibi?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2142-->
<!--Post: 2429--><!--Time: 1103658962-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2429"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 11:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->any more info on that Oliver? <BR> <BR>B<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2429-->
<!--Post: 4377--><!--Time: 1106264517-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4377"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Miamom<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Miamom<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 20, 2005 - 3:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sounds logical.  I haven&#39;t posted here before but over a AMW.  Too many cranks over there.  I feel that BTK is a momma&#39;s boy.  A comment that Dennis made also, brought this home. I know a Momma&#39;s boy that has many similarities to what BTK has written about, but I know they are not the same.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4377-->
<!--Post: 4393--><!--Time: 1106300642-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4393"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Deedle<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Deedle<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 1:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Considering they can use the DNA evidence now, I highly doubt they would continue to rule someone out just because their MOTHER gave an alibi.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4393-->
<!--Post: 6777--><!--Time: 1108003053-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6777"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 6:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I remember the Poet thing from when I was a kid.  I really freaked a lot of people out.  I had tried to research the case on the net, but could not for the life of me remember the lady&#39;s name, so thans Ksugirl for the post...that helps a lot.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6777-->
<!--Post: 6795--><!--Time: 1108009883-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6795"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksugirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksugirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Neechi, you and I must be about the same age, because I remember the Poet from my childhood also. My family was new to Wichita at the time, and my parents were quite unsettled about it.  The book is great, but heartbreaking, to read.   <BR> <BR>KSUGirl  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6795-->
<!--Post: 8459--><!--Time: 1109147662-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8459"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dsv<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dsv<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 12:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->FYI <BR> <BR>LE finally discovered she was the sender of letters after they observed her mailing the letters to herself as she dropped them into a public mail box. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8459-->
</table></td></tr></table>
